# Home Assistant writes its entire working state into `config/`, including
# `.storage`, which holds this instance's users and long-lived tokens. None of
# it belongs in a public repo, and the demo is meant to be rebuilt rather than
# preserved - deleting the directory is the reset.
#
# Ignore everything under `config/` and re-admit only what we author, so the
# next file Home Assistant decides to write is excluded by default rather than
# committed by whoever runs `git add` next.
config/*
!config/configuration.yaml

# Where the run puts the token and ids it discovers, so the seed and screenshot
# steps can be run separately without redoing onboarding.
.demo-session.json

# Written when a screenshot run fails, to show where the browser had got to.
# Evidence for whoever is debugging, never something to keep.
failure.png
